# Laptop Exec — SSH-First (auto)

Projects under `~/mounts/` are SSHFS from the laptop. **Mount may be STALE or NOT_MOUNTED.**
Tunnel SSH via `laptop-exec` still works. **Do not ask the user to mention laptop-exec.**

## Start every task

```bash
laptop-exec status
laptop-exec health
```

When `tunnel: UP` → **100% agent work through laptop-exec** (read, write, rg, git, run).

## BLOCKED on /mounts/ (hook enforced)

| Tool / shell | Use instead |
|--------------|-------------|
| Read | `laptop-exec read [-p P] file` |
| Write | `laptop-exec write [-p P] file` (stdin) |
| Grep / Glob | `laptop-exec rg [-p P] pattern` |
| git, find, build in shell | `laptop-exec git` / `laptop-exec run` |

## Project selection

1. `-p PROJECT`
2. `-w ~/mounts/PROJECT/...` when Agent cwd is not under mounts (hook blocks Read)
3. cwd under `~/mounts/PROJECT/` (auto)
4. `LAPTOP_EXEC_WORKSPACE` env / `laptop-exec resolve [path]`
5. `ACTIVE_MOUNT` from connect session

When workspace folder name != `active_mount` → **must use `-p`**.

## Quick commands

```bash
laptop-exec list              # fast; list --full for sshfs per project
laptop-exec mount-status -p PROJECT
laptop-exec read scripts/foo.sh
laptop-exec write scripts/foo.sh <<'EOF'
...
EOF
laptop-exec git -- status
laptop-exec rg Pattern
laptop-exec run -- dotnet build
```

## tunnel DOWN

Tell user to run connect.bat/sh. No project operations until tunnel UP.
